  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinS&E 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A pharmaceutical company is sponsoring a clinical trial across several
    cancer centers. The company is responsible for funding the study, ensuring it
    follows regulations, and reporting study results.


    <b>Which authority is
    primarily responsible for overseeing the trial at this level?</b>'
  explanation: The study sponsor funds and oversees the overall conduct of the trial,
    ensuring regulatory requirements are met and the study is managed consistently
    across all sites. They help coordinate the research team, monitor progress, and
    make sure the trial follows approved plans and timelines.
  correctAnswer: Study sponsor
  incorrectAnswer1: Scientific Review Committee (SRC)
  incorrectAnswer2: Institutional Review Board (IRB)
  incorrectAnswer3: Data and Safety Monitoring Board (DSMB)
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
